00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:57.480
Now, I've told you the two main reasons why this&nbsp;
entire separate into two countries won't work. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:03.840
first is the unconstitutionality of unilateral&nbsp;
secession. Now, maybe Marjorie. Maybe Marjorie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.440
Taylor GREENE is talking about a version where,&nbsp;
like, everybody agrees. Everybody's like, No,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.940
you're like Oklahoma. You should go. Go do&nbsp;
your own thing. But the Constitution of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:17.280
United States, which is the supreme law of the&nbsp;
land, doesn't provide a provision for secession.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:24.300
And in fact, the idea of secession arguably was&nbsp;
tested in the Civil War. Supreme Court has ruled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:30.180
you can't just secede. States can't just say we&nbsp;
secede. It's not a legal option for any state.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:37.080
If you attempt to do it, you would be violating&nbsp;
the Constitution and Supreme Court rulings. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:42.180
the second part of it is that the red states&nbsp;
aren't viable as a country. And I know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.900
if you watched last week's show, you already&nbsp;
know this. But I do want to get it into this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:52.740
clip as well. The red state country that would be&nbsp;
created is fundamentally not viable economically.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:57.900
And this is for a number of different reasons.&nbsp;
GDP per capita is much lower in red states than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:04.740
blue states. Red states are disproportionately&nbsp;
subsidized with federal funding that comes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:11.940
blue states which overwhelmingly pay money in&nbsp;
rather than get money out. Blue states, on average&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:19.680
have more diverse economies, whereas red states&nbsp;
often depend on one industry or product or sector.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:26.400
So it's very at risk to that one. You know, oil in&nbsp;
Texas or agriculture in Kansas. So that makes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:33.060
economies generally more vulnerable to economic&nbsp;
fluctuations. There are, on average, more educated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.560
people in the blue states. That leads to higher&nbsp;
paying jobs and more innovation. There's better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:43.980
infrastructure as a result in the blue states.&nbsp;
Education and access to health care tend to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:49.260
better, which also makes it more attractive for&nbsp;
businesses. It's a vicious cycle, and right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:55.860
to a great degree, the red states are being pulled&nbsp;
up by all of these aspects of blue states. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:02.040
you've just got red states as a country, it really&nbsp;
wouldn't work well at all. And Mitt Romney just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:07.500
